  "worked_solution": "First, we factor the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{{sin}^{5}\u2061\\theta +{sin}^{3}\u2061\\theta {cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }=\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{{sin}^{3}\u2061\\theta \\cdot ({sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta +{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta )}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{{sin}^{3}\u2061\\theta \\cdot ({sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta +{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta )} & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{{sin}^{3}\u2061\\theta \\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{{sin}^{3}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}\u2061\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{{sin}^{5}\u2061\\theta +{sin}^{3}\u2061\\theta {cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }=\\operatorname{cot}\u2061\\theta .\n$$",
